WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.384 --> 00:00:18.745
My name is Robby, and this is my friend Zack.

2
00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:22.384
"Hi! It's nice to meet you."

3
00:00:22.384 --> 00:00:24.743
Zack moved here three years ago.

4
00:00:24.743 --> 00:00:34.039
I still remember his first day in our classroom.

5
00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:39.525
A woman was with him.

6
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:42.595
"I'm Mrs. Ray," the woman said.

7
00:00:42.595 --> 00:00:45.664
She explained that Zack is deaf.

8
00:00:45.664 --> 00:00:47.458
"I'm an interpreter.

9
00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:51.898
My job is to help Zack learn and communicate at school."

10
00:00:51.898 --> 00:00:56.140
I raised my hand. "Does Zack read lips?"

11
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.668
"Yes," said Mrs. Ray. "And he wears hearing aids.

12
00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:06.197
In the classroom he and I will use sign language to communicate."

13
00:01:06.197 --> 00:01:08.959
Soon our teacher began a math lesson.

14
00:01:08.959 --> 00:01:12.496
I watched Mrs. Ray explaining things to Zack.

15
00:01:12.497 --> 00:01:16.886
They both moved their arms and hands fast.

16
00:01:16.886 --> 00:01:21.406
Their faces changed expression a lot.

17
00:01:21.406 --> 00:01:26.377
"Wow," I thought. "Sign language is cool!"

18
00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:30.367
Zack and I sat together every day in the cafeteria.

19
00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.905
Zack got really good at reading my lips.

20
00:01:33.905 --> 00:01:38.957
I could tell because he always laughed at my jokes!

21
00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:42.934
One day Mom and I started planning my sleepover party.

22
00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.888
I looked down at the guest list.

23
00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:49.186
"What's wrong, Robby?" asked Mom.

24
00:01:49.186 --> 00:01:50.975
"I want to invite Zack.

25
00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:54.946
But it will be hard for him when everyone is talking or playing games.

26
00:01:54.946 --> 00:01:56.683
He'll feel left out.

27
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.768
I wish I could talk with him more easily."

28
00:01:59.768 --> 00:02:02.476
"Hmm," said Mom.

29
00:02:02.476 --> 00:02:08.542
"I saw a poster about a sign language class at the library. Want to go?"

30
00:02:08.542 --> 00:02:11.429
"Yes!"

31
00:02:11.429 --> 00:02:15.139
Mom and I went to the sign language class together.

32
00:02:15.139 --> 00:02:19.580
We found out there are many different kinds of sign languages.

33
00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:27.094
All sign languages use hand, face, and body movements to communicate words and ideas.

34
00:02:27.094 --> 00:02:31.121
Mom and I learned American Sign Language.

35
00:02:31.121 --> 00:02:34.275
First, we learned simple words.

36
00:02:34.275 --> 00:02:39.073
Hello. Good-bye. Thank you.

37
00:02:39.073 --> 00:02:42.095
Then we learned the alphabet.

38
00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.777
A, B, C.

39
00:02:45.777 --> 00:02:49.597
Soon we were signing sentences!

40
00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:52.518
How are you?

41
00:02:52.518 --> 00:02:55.726
It's raining today.

42
00:02:55.726 --> 00:03:01.674
I couldn't wait until my sleepover party.

43
00:03:01.674 --> 00:03:05.476
When Zack arrived, I was waiting at the door.

44
00:03:05.476 --> 00:03:09.055
"Hi, Zack. Thank you for coming."

45
00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:18.959
Zack grinned. "You know sign language, Robby! Awesome!"

46
00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:21.342
I'm still learning sign language.

47
00:03:21.343 --> 00:03:25.000
But I've gotten really good at talking with my buddy Zack.

48
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.549
Now I can laugh at his dumb jokes!

49
00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:33.540
"What fish only swims at night?

50
00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:42.036
A starfish!"
